// EXPECT: PASS
// Scope guard for the 2026-07-21 middle-option: modeling the integer parameters of a NON-contract
// function must not degrade into a blanket reject of param asserts — a genuinely PROVABLE assert must
// stay green. `x >= 0` holds for every value the runtime can produce for a `u8` parameter: a `u8` is
// masked to [0, 2^8) at the call boundary (`anubis_coerce_uint_param`), a range the checker soundly
// injects, so the assert is discharged. The signed tautology `y == y` is proven for any i64 `y`. Both
// match `run`, which never traps. If this fixture ever flips to FAIL, the middle-option has started
// over-rejecting provable param asserts.
pub fn safe(x: u8, y: int) {
    assert(x >= 0);
    assert(y == y);
}

fn main() {
    safe(200, 7);
}
